(2719107, 370914, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>   Nice action and great story! The color and lighting look good. I think it does well with the motion blur. Probably it just didn''t have enough "wow" for a higher score.</td>', 'Trading post...   Nice action and great story! The color and lighting look good. I think it does well with the motion blur. Probably it just didn''t have enough "wow" for a higher score.', '2006-08-11 20:08:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2719824, 370497, 26906, '<td valign="top">I agree with you 100%. In addition to numerous sporting events where I was accredited, I shot US Open tennis professionaly from 2000 to 2002. It is certainly exciting, technically challenging and labor-intensive, but has nothing to do with art.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> people voted low for dnmc because they wanted the entire challenge to be sports shots so that I would be bored to death. this is a great picture in a challenge that was way too boring for me to vote on. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'I agree with you 100%. In addition to numerous sporting events where I was accredited, I shot US Open tennis professionaly from 2000 to 2002. It is certainly exciting, technically challenging and labor-intensive, but has nothing to do with art. Originally posted by posthumous: people voted low for dnmc because they wanted the entire challenge to be sports shots so that I would be bored to death. this is a great picture in a challenge that was way too boring for me to vote on. ', '2006-08-12 02:41:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2720745, 373438, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading post comment<br/> <br/>Major congrats, Eric, on your 5th place finish.  I love this shot.  I agree with Melethia that his expression really makes this photo, but I also think the angle of the kiyak, with the dunking he is about to get, make this photo stand out, too.  Superb shot.</td>', 'Trading post comment Major congrats, Eric, on your 5th place finish.  I love this shot.  I agree with Melethia that his expression really makes this photo, but I also think the angle of the kiyak, with the dunking he is about to get, make this photo stand out, too.  Superb shot.', '2006-08-12 15:02:37.000000', NULL, 0),
