(2752191, 372059, 27181, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Haneck:</b></div><hr/><i> Amazing! everything else is a blur - but the subject is clear enough to be distinguished! How many shots did it take you to get that? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi. Thanks! Actually, I think it took me about 10 shots. This is the clearest I got. Pretty crappy hands huh?! Hehe.</td>', 'Originally posted by Haneck: Amazing! everything else is a blur - but the subject is clear enough to be distinguished! How many shots did it take you to get that?   Hi. Thanks! Actually, I think it took me about 10 shots. This is the clearest I got. Pretty crappy hands huh?! Hehe.', '2006-08-23 10:58:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2761443, 373470, 40106, '<td valign="top">COOOOL! i love the composition!!  the sky looks a bit grainy... perhaps a little noise reduction might help??</td>', 'COOOOL! i love the composition!!  the sky looks a bit grainy... perhaps a little noise reduction might help??', '2006-08-26 02:11:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2761598, 371865, 13077, '<td valign="top">The composition and angle are ok, except for the tower in the background.. sometimes with busy backgrounds you have to either get closer with a wider lens, or farther away with a long one.. it all depends on the scene and how much time you have I guess. I probably would have shot it from the other side of the bowl with a longer lens, which by the looks of the lighting means you''d have to use flash (most skate/bmx photos are shot using flash, partly since the right angle is more important than the right light, and flashes are more portable than the sun)</td>', 'The composition and angle are ok, except for the tower in the background.. sometimes with busy backgrounds you have to either get closer with a wider lens, or farther away with a long one.. it all depends on the scene and how much time you have I guess. I probably would have shot it from the other side of the bowl with a longer lens, which by the looks of the lighting means you''d have to use flash (most skate/bmx photos are shot using flash, partly since the right angle is more important than the right light, and flashes are more portable than the sun)', '2006-08-26 03:28:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2769698, 373761, 58537, '<td valign="top">Natural light was on the wrong side to bring out their chests,  a shutter of 1/500th would stop it better on their fingers, but the bit of motion blur adds to the speed of their motions.  Not knowing how far you were from the players, a strobe might have punched up your subjects contrast and using a rear sync on that flash puts the motion blur behind the direction of motion and makes then more natural.</td>', 'Natural light was on the wrong side to bring out their chests,  a shutter of 1/500th would stop it better on their fingers, but the bit of motion blur adds to the speed of their motions.  Not knowing how far you were from the players, a strobe might have punched up your subjects contrast and using a rear sync on that flash puts the motion blur behind the direction of motion and makes then more natural.', '2006-08-29 04:14:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2786482, 372662, 40667, '<td valign="top">Very Nice! being a rugby player i alwayse love seeing the shots!<br/>thanks for sharing it here!</td>', 'Very Nice! being a rugby player i alwayse love seeing the shots!thanks for sharing it here!', '2006-09-02 01:42:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2786767, 370179, 60862, '<td valign="top">Wow.  Lightning shots are always cool, but this is truly incredible.  Your framing with the foreground pole is good, and the colors are very nice.<br/> <br/>But what makes me really gawk is the tiny power poles on the horizon.  I''m glad you pointed them out, because you''re right:  they really give a sense of the enormity of lightning and the raw power they represent.<br/> <br/>Going in my favorites to keep your other shots in there company. :)</td>', 'Wow.  Lightning shots are always cool, but this is truly incredible.  Your framing with the foreground pole is good, and the colors are very nice. But what makes me really gawk is the tiny power poles on the horizon.  I''m glad you pointed them out, because you''re right:  they really give a sense of the enormity of lightning and the raw power they represent. Going in my favorites to keep your other shots in there company. :)', '2006-09-02 03:27:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2788651, 373327, 30982, '<td valign="top">Great shot - wonderful lines and toning and excellent action.  Nice of you to let your son come in ahead of you, too.</td>', 'Great shot - wonderful lines and toning and excellent action.  Nice of you to let your son come in ahead of you, too.', '2006-09-02 15:26:13.000000', NULL, 0),
